# Landing & marketing — decisions

## Logged-out surface
**Chose:** Render a standalone marketing page for logged-out visitors; redirect linked users directly to Results.
**Why:** ⚠️ NEEDS INPUT — `src/routes/index.tsx` establishes the split, but no rationale for bypassing the app shell was found.

## Marketing-specific visual system
**Chose:** Use a zinc-black, indigo, and violet landing palette separate from the application’s canvas tokens.
**Why:** ⚠️ NEEDS INPUT — `LandingPage.tsx` and `landing.css` make the divergence clear, but no rationale was found.

## Hero depth
**Chose:** Build the hero parallax with CSS perspective and `translateZ` layers.
**Considered:** JavaScript scroll listeners.
**Why:** The header comment in `landing.css` explicitly says “CSS 3D parallax (no scroll listeners).”

## Chess metaphor
**Chose:** Show an Italian position on the hero board and animate selected pieces lifting away as “leaks.”
**Why:** `LandingBoardPieces.tsx` documents the position and calls the lifted pieces “the leaks.”

## Motion accessibility
**Chose:** Remove positional animation and flatten the parallax scene for reduced-motion users; remove glass effects for reduced-transparency users.
**Why:** ⚠️ NEEDS INPUT — the accessibility fallbacks are explicit in `landing.css`, but no rationale comment was found.

## Conversion paths
**Chose:** Lead with Sign up, then offer Free game review and a fixed-player Preview.
**Why:** ⚠️ NEEDS INPUT — the CTA hierarchy is implemented in `LandingPage.tsx` without documented rationale.

## Product proof
**Chose:** Reuse an actual chess position, classification badge, and guess-before-reveal preview rather than static marketing screenshots.
**Why:** ⚠️ NEEDS INPUT — `HeroPosition` and `/preview` implement live product artifacts, but no rationale was found.
